fork-linux (1.0.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Open in: every IDE entry shows the IDE's own icon (taken from its
    desktop entry and written into the fl-launch stub Fork reads).
  * Crisp, evenly spaced interface text: the interface font is Noto Sans
    2.015 (pinned faces, installed renamed as FL UI Sans) instead of
    Selawik, whose hinting spaced letters unevenly under Wine; semibold
    and bold text keep their weight.
  * Not affiliated with Fork's developers; buy Fork at https://git-fork.com/buy.

 -- Sergiu Alexandrescu <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000

fork-linux (1.0.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Open in: stubs now sit exactly where Fork probes, so IntelliJ IDEA,
    PyCharm, WebStorm, PhpStorm, Rider, GoLand, Sublime Text and Atom are
    listed (only VS Code, Insiders and Cursor were before); add GoLand,
    Fleet, Zed, Antigravity, Antigravity IDE and CodeBuddy.
  * Snap IDEs start again (the snap launcher is no longer resolved to
    snapd); Flatpak apps and JetBrains Toolbox scripts are found too.
  * Editor options (-g FILE:LINE) reach the IDE; Android Studio stubs,
    which Fork never lists, are removed.
  * Includes 1.0.3 (not published on its own): repo fix/undo default to
    every repository Fork knows, so Stage All works under Wine.
  * ruff 0.17.1; Arch CI base 20261011.0.609700.
  * Not affiliated with Fork's developers; buy Fork at https://git-fork.com/buy.

 -- Sergiu Alexandrescu <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

